---
// D-10 (04-08 Task 3): /about — v1's current text (915tldr.com2/app/pages/about.vue) carried over
// verbatim, converted from Vue/Tailwind template markup to plain semantic HTML inside the same
// narrow reading column contact.html's mockup already established (`[data-contact-column]` is a
// standalone narrow-column style, not paired to the rail layout — confirmed against
// design/mockups/style.css before reuse). No wording changed (Phase 10 rewrites About —
// IDNT-01/02); decorative-only markup (background noise texture, divider icons, drop-cap letter
// spans) is dropped since it carries no visible text, but every heading, paragraph and list item
// is preserved, including the drop-cap's own letter reunited with the rest of its sentence.
//
// One internal link omitted, not reworded: v1's "Our Sources" paragraph ends with a
// "View our sources →" link to `/sources`. No such route exists in this build (only per-source
// pages at `/source/<slug>` — 04-05) — linking to it would ship a dead internal link. The
// surrounding sentence's own wording is unchanged; only the dead CTA phrase itself is omitted.
// See 04-08-SUMMARY.md.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  page="about"
  title="About 915 TLDR"
  description="Learn about 915 TLDR, the AI-powered news aggregator for El Paso, Texas. How we work and our mission to simplify local news."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <div data-contact-column>
    <p data-eyebrow>Est. 2025 · El Paso, Texas</p>
    <h1>About 915 TLDR</h1>
    <p data-lede>
      Your AI-powered window into El Paso news—aggregated, summarized, and organized for the way
      you read today.
    </p>

    <h2>What does "TLDR" mean?</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>TLDR</strong> stands for <strong>"Too Long; Didn't Read"</strong>—internet shorthand
      for a quick summary. When something is too long to read in full, you ask for the TLDR: just
      the essential points.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's exactly what we do with El Paso news. We read it all so you don't have to, then give
      you the TLDR.
    </p>

    <h2>Our Mission</h2>
    <p>
      We believe staying informed about your community shouldn't feel like a chore. 915 TLDR
      automatically collects news from El Paso's most trusted local sources, uses AI to extract
      key insights, and presents everything in a clean, scannable format.
    </p>
    <p>
      No more hopping between websites. No more clickbait headlines. Just the news that matters to
      El Paso, delivered the way modern readers want it—fast, clear, and comprehensive.
    </p>

    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>Smart features that make local news accessible</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>AI Summaries</dt>
      <dd>Get the key points from every story without reading the full article.</dd>
      <dt>Multi-Source Coverage</dt>
      <dd>See how different outlets cover the same story, all in one place.</dd>
      <dt>Categorized Content</dt>
      <dd>Browse by topic—politics, crime, sports, business, and more.</dd>
      <dt>Full-Text Search</dt>
      <dd>Find any article on any topic with powerful search.</dd>
      <dt>Mobile Friendly</dt>
      <dd>Read comfortably on any device, anywhere.</dd>
      <dt>Always Updated</dt>
      <dd>Fresh news automatically collected every few hours.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Our Sources</h2>
    <p>
      We aggregate content from El Paso's most trusted local news organizations. Every story links
      back to its original source—we're here to help you discover news, not replace the
      journalists who report it.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions or Feedback?</h2>
    <p>
      We'd love to hear from you. Whether you have suggestions for new sources, found a bug, or
      just want to say hello—reach out.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/contact">Get in Touch</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
